# Architecture Pack

Use when changing component boundaries, ownership, or major dependency relationships.

- Explain the concrete need, relevant constraints, credible alternatives, and cost of the proposed boundary change.
- Identify who owns behavior, data, dependencies, and recovery. Preserve project conventions unless a change is justified.
- Justify new layers, services, abstractions, and dependencies with an actual requirement; do not impose a universal architecture style.
- Use grill-me when an available workflow can resolve a contested consequential assumption; accept settled decisions without new evidence.
- Record a decision only when it will help future work, using an existing project format when present. Define evidence or conditions that would justify revisiting it.
